.th NARGS III 5/10/73
.sh NAME
nargs \*- argument count
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd "nargs( )"
.sh DESCRIPTION
.it Nargs
returns the number of actual parameters
supplied by the caller of the routine which calls 
\fInargs\fR.
.s3
The argument count is accurate only when
none of the actual parameters is
.it float
or
\fIdouble\fR.
Such parameters count as four arguments instead of one.
.sh BUGS
As indicated.
Also, this routine may not work in programs
with separated I and D space, unless a minor
hardware alteration has been made
on the machine itself (to enable mfpi user\->user
to work)!
